# PSR-4b-configure — product-adapter hygiene (partial)

## Scope

| Work | Done |
| --- | --- |
| Inventory all `apps/api/src/http/configure-*.ts` | Yes (4) |
| Rename finance wiring to platform-neutral filename | Yes |
| Retarget denali/urban configure imports `/http` → `/host/http` | Yes |
| Add tsconfig `host/http` path mappings | Yes |
| Delete denali/urban product-named configure files | **No** |
| Expire tsconfig bare `/http` aliases (tests) | **Yes** — see [`psr-4b-http-alias.mdoc`](./psr-4b-http-alias.mdoc) |

Land commit: `86e22b6d`

Machine inventory:
[`psr-4b-configure-inventory.yaml`](./psr-4b-configure-inventory.yaml)

## Classification

| Path | Class | Why |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `configure-finance-http-host.ts` | `platform-neutral` | Wires `@app-tour/finance-http` only |
| `configure-workspace-denali-product-http-host.ts` | `product-named` | Denali HTTP host ports |
| `configure-urban-http-host.ts` | `product-named` | Urban HTTP host ports |
| `configure-urban-surface-exposure.ts` | `product-named` | Urban exposure resolver |

## Why finance rename counts

SoT §PSR-4.4: product-named configure modules should leave the host.
Finance was already **content-neutral** (`@app-tour/finance-http`) but still named
`configure-workspace-finance-http-host`. Rename removes false product gravity
without moving host infrastructure into workspace packages.

## Why denali/urban not deleted this wave

Those adapters inject host ports (`TourStorageDbAdapter`, idempotency, tenant
kernel, booking public adapter). True absorption needs a generated bootstrap or
neutral port registry — deferred to **PSR-4b-configure-2**.

## Bare `/http` vs `/host/http`

Encapsulation already maps `@app-tour/workspace-*/http` → `/host/http`.
Configure adapters now follow that map. `apps/api/tsconfig.json` still carries
compat aliases for **tests** that import bare `/http`; expiry is a follow-on.

## Ratchet

```bash
node scripts/ops/psr-4b-configure-smoke.mjs
```

| Metric | Ceiling |
| --- | ---: |
| product-named configure files | **3** |
| bare `/http` imports inside configure-* | **0** |

## Explicit non-goals

- Harbor configure (none today)
- Moving exposure logic into `workspace-urban` package
- Deleting tsconfig `/http` aliases while tests still use them
